WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.542
The teaching database intentionally contains imperfect data.

00:00:03.542 --> 00:00:08.662
Customers includes formatting differences, missing values, and duplicates.

00:00:08.662 --> 00:00:13.882
Products includes inconsistent categories and invalid numeric values.

00:00:13.882 --> 00:00:18.992
Messy customers is a staging table designed for the integrated cleaning project.

00:00:18.992 --> 00:00:26.757
The problems are deliberate so that we can practice detection and resolution instead of working with

00:00:26.757 --> 00:00:32.362
already-perfect data. Connect this idea to a customer master-data project cleaning duplicate profiles.

00:00:32.362 --> 00:00:38.302
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:38.302 --> 00:00:46.212
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:52.207
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:52.207 --> 00:00:58.150
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
